*__pycache__
.venv*
.claude

# --- model artifacts ---
model/saved/test_*

# --- hardware: simulation artifacts ---
accel/tpu/sim/obj_dir/
accel/tpu/sim/*.vcd
accel/tpu/sim/*.fst
accel/tpu/sim/*.wdb
accel/tpu/sim/*.vvp
accel/tpu/sim/*.out

# tb/Makefile writes compiled/waveform output next to the testbenches, not into
# sim/. (Some of these are already tracked from before this rule existed —
# `git rm --cached accel/tpu/tb/*.vvp accel/tpu/tb/*.vcd` to drop them.)
accel/tpu/tb/*.vvp
accel/tpu/tb/*.vcd
accel/tpu/tb/*.fst

# `make cosim` (host/sim_link.py) builds the testbench and both halves of its
# host<->device byte stream here.
accel/tpu/tb/cosim/

# --- hardware: synthesis / place-and-route / bitstreams ---
accel/tpu/synth/build/
*.bit
*.bin
*.jou
*.log

# --- hardware: Vivado ---
# No Vivado *project* is version controlled. synth/vivado/build.tcl is the
# recipe; everything it produces goes to synth/build/<board>/ (ignored above).
# The rest of these catch the debris Vivado drops into whatever directory it
# happens to be launched from, which is often the repo root.
*.xpr
*.xpr.bak
.Xil/
.srcs/
*.cache/
*.gen/
*.hw/
*.ip_user_files/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.dcp
*.mcs
*.prm
*.ltx
*.str
usage_statistics_webtalk.*
tight_setup_hold_pins.txt
hs_err_pid*.log
clockInfo.txt
